From 1bbf23225e7e0cf092abe0e8e1f20382ef388495 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 21:00:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: rebuild profile 5 and map it to SDR where the
 output takes no HDR10

Dolby Vision as HDR10 left a stream whose base layer is no picture by itself
(profile 5, and profile 10 with compatibility 0) to Kodi's ordinary output
where the output takes no HDR10 (an SDR display, the panel of a laptop, a TV
without HDR, or Kodi's HDR output turned off): its IPTPQc2 base layer is then
shown as a YCbCr picture, green and purple. Profiles 7 and 8.1 do not change
there: their base layer is the HDR10 version of the studio, which Kodi takes to
SDR as it takes any HDR10 picture.

DVBRIDGE::ConversionTargetOf() says what a stream is reconstructed for: HDR10
exactly where ConversionEligible() said so before, on an output that takes it;
on one that takes none, SDR, for such a stream only, whatever the settings of
the conversion to HDR10 say (they are settings of HDR10 outputs, and the base
layer as Kodi shows it is no picture to choose), and never with the user's
choice of Kodi's own output for the video (which is not offered for such a
stream), software decoding, interlaced or stereoscopic video. The window system
says when an SDR target can be had (SupportsDVConversionToSdr(), looked at for
each video with the HDR10 one); the decoder keeps the metadata of the pictures
and marks them (VideoPicture::doviConvertSdr); the renderer sets the output up
for an SDR picture of BT.709 at the depth of the stream, as Kodi sets it up for
the base layer, and has the bridge draw the picture with dvbridge_sdr_mapping().

It fails closed as the conversion to HDR10 does: an output that takes HDR
signalling for such a picture, a mapping that the bridge does not take (then
nothing is drawn: a picture as mastered, in PQ, is no picture on an SDR output
either) or 48 pictures in a row that cannot be rebuilt, and the video plays as
Kodi plays it. A picture that cannot be rebuilt shows the last whole one again,
also after a seek: its base layer is never shown instead
(DVBRIDGE::ConversionShowsBase() holds for no profile 5 stream and no mapped
picture). The depth of the output is not asked about such a picture (the
question is that of HDR signalling).

The player information says "Dolby Vision rebuilt, mapped to SDR" (#31713, in
en_gb, es_es, es_ar and es_mx) with the layers of the picture, and
VideoPlayer.HdrDetail ends in "SDR" instead of "HDR10".

The rule is tested on the host (8072 checks over 2688 combinations of output,
settings, choice, profile and stream; three mutations of it caught). The
picture is measured with the bridge on the software OpenGL ES (the commit of the
bridge). The rest is compiled in syntax-only mode and read; none of it has run
in Kodi or on a display.
